<p class="note">
    Pick a verse to see its connections.
</p>
<p>
    This tool uses the cross-references from
    <a href="https://github.com/CrossReferences-org/bible-cross-references">crossreferences.org</a>,
    which build on the Treasury of Scripture Knowledge. The difference here is that we follow
    the connections further down the chain, which surfaces more cross-references and a
    hopefully better ordering. It sometimes also adds context verses alongside the ones
    directly referenced.
</p>
<p>
    The scoring and the indicators evolve continuously, so they aren't documented in detail.
    Roughly, each level contributes less to the final score than the one before it:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>L1</b>: Direct references in this verse</li>
    <li><b>Incoming</b>: Verses which reference this verse</li>
    <li><b>L2</b>: References found for verses in L1</li>
    <li><b>L3</b>: References found for verses in L2</li>
</ul>
<p>
    Best is to play around and understand it by using it.
</p>